# The production STACK's settings (docs/100 §3) — not the API's: those are in the API env file named below.
# Copy to deploy/production/stack.env on the host (git-ignored) and fill in. Nothing here is a secret.
#
# Two profiles share deploy/docker-compose.production.yml, and lib.sh enforces each one's values:
#   production  project erp-production, paths under /srv/erp-production, API_HOST=api.tsxmr.com, edge on 80/443
#   rehearsal   project erp-rehearsal,  paths under /srv/erp-rehearsal,  API_HOST=*.localhost, edge on 127.0.0.1 only
DEPLOY_PROFILE=production

# The public API hostname. Its DNS record points at this host, DNS only (not proxied): docs/100 §6.
API_HOST=api.tsxmr.com
# Where certificate notices go (ACME account). An address that is read.
ACME_EMAIL=developer@tsxmr.com

# The published ports of the edge, the only published ports of the stack. Production: 80 and 443 on every address.
EDGE_HTTP_BIND=80
EDGE_HTTPS_BIND=443

# Owned by the deployment account, mode 700, outside the checkout. setup-secrets.sh fills it (db/, api/, the two
# connection files); the owner's SMTP login and key go to api/ through a hidden prompt. Never in a backup.
SECRETS_DIR=/srv/erp-production/secrets
# Encrypted backups (age), their checksums, deployments.log and current-images.env. Copied off the host (docs/100 §5).
BACKUP_DIR=/srv/erp-production/backups
# The API's environment: a copy of .env.production.example, filled in, mode 600, outside the checkout. No secret.
API_ENV_FILE=/srv/erp-production/api.env
